WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.277
Soon Tom stopped worrying about the murder because he had something else to worry about—Becky.

2
00:00:06.278 --> 00:00:09.507
She was sick, and Tom thought she might die.

3
00:00:09.508 --> 00:00:14.991
Tom was so worried about Becky that he stopped playing with his friends.

4
00:00:14.992 --> 00:00:19.228
One day Tom waited outside Becky's house, hoping to see her.

5
00:00:19.229 --> 00:00:22.266
When he didn't spot her at all, he was sad.

6
00:00:22.267 --> 00:00:24.844
Aunt Polly worried about Tom too.

7
00:00:24.845 --> 00:00:30.355
To make Tom feel better, she tried lots of new remedies that she read about in a women's magazine.

8
00:00:30.356 --> 00:00:34.916
One remedy was giving Tom a cold bath every evening.

9
00:00:34.917 --> 00:00:39.932
Afterward Aunt Polly would wrap him in many layers of blankets until he began to sweat.

10
00:00:39.933 --> 00:00:44.855
The treatment didn't help. It only made Tom quieter and sadder.

11
00:00:44.856 --> 00:00:50.273
Next Aunt Polly talked to her friends, and they recommended a medicine made from chili peppers.

12
00:00:50.274 --> 00:00:54.066
Aunt Polly decided to try it on Tom.

13
00:00:54.067 --> 00:00:59.938
She gave Tom a teaspoon of the medicine and watched his face.

14
00:00:59.939 --> 00:01:04.909
Tom's mouth, throat, and stomach felt as if they were on fire.

15
00:01:04.910 --> 00:01:07.662
He screamed and ran around the room.

16
00:01:07.663 --> 00:01:12.204
Aunt Polly was pleased because Tom was finally acting like himself again.

17
00:01:12.205 --> 00:01:16.576
She told Tom that if he didn't feel better tomorrow, she'd give him more medicine.

18
00:01:16.577 --> 00:01:19.694
Tom quickly decided to be less sad!

19
00:01:19.695 --> 00:01:22.870
Tom wondered what else the medicine could cure.

20
00:01:22.871 --> 00:01:26.533
The cat, for example, was suffering from laziness.

21
00:01:26.534 --> 00:01:31.554
The medicine had made Tom more active, so maybe it would make the cat more active too!

22
00:01:31.555 --> 00:01:35.257
Tom gave some hot chili pepper medicine to the cat.

23
00:01:35.258 --> 00:01:41.250
The cat leaped into the air, screamed, and ran around and around the room.

24
00:01:41.251 --> 00:01:44.816
He knocked over chairs, plants, and book shelves.

25
00:01:44.817 --> 00:01:48.246
Tom thought it was the funniest thing he had ever seen.

26
00:01:48.247 --> 00:01:52.575
Aunt Polly came into the room just as the cat jumped out the window.

27
00:01:52.576 --> 00:01:56.130
"What's wrong with the cat?" asked Aunt Polly.

28
00:01:56.131 --> 00:01:59.295
Tom was laughing too hard to answer.

29
00:01:59.296 --> 00:02:03.420
Aunt Polly saw the teaspoon and the medicine bottle on the floor.

30
00:02:03.421 --> 00:02:07.869
"How could you treat the cat like that?" she asked sternly.

31
00:02:07.870 --> 00:02:14.452
Tom said, "The cat's been lazy, and you don't love him enough, so I felt sorry for him.

32
00:02:14.453 --> 00:02:20.008
I decided to love the cat like you love me. I gave him some medicine."

33
00:02:20.009 --> 00:02:22.976
Tom's words made Aunt Polly feel bad.

34
00:02:22.977 --> 00:02:26.478
She hadn't meant to be unloving, so she apologized.

35
00:02:26.479 --> 00:02:29.785
She explained she only wanted Tom to feel better.

36
00:02:29.786 --> 00:02:34.634
Tom smiled and said, "I know you meant well, and it worked.

37
00:02:34.635 --> 00:02:37.545
I think the medicine helped the cat too.

38
00:02:37.546 --> 00:02:42.612
I've never seen him move so fast."

39
00:02:42.613 --> 00:02:48.766
Tom was still smiling about the cat when he got to school, but his amusement soon turned to delight.

40
00:02:48.767 --> 00:02:53.554
Becky was back! Tom tried everything to get Becky's attention.

41
00:02:53.555 --> 00:02:59.891
He jumped over the fence; he walked on his hands; he even did cartwheels off the school steps.

42
00:02:59.892 --> 00:03:04.027
But Becky was still mad about Tom being engaged to Amy first.

43
00:03:04.028 --> 00:03:11.506
Ignoring Tom, she turned to a friend and said loudly, "Some people think they're so smart, always showing off!"

44
00:03:11.507 --> 00:03:14.940
Tom was so angry that he ran into the woods.

45
00:03:14.941 --> 00:03:19.812
There he met his friend Joe Harper. Joe was angry too.

46
00:03:19.813 --> 00:03:23.808
His mother had punished him for something he didn't do.

47
00:03:23.809 --> 00:03:29.718
Tom had an idea. "Let's run away. That will make them sorry."

48
00:03:29.719 --> 00:03:33.224
Joe agreed and said he would like to live on an island.

49
00:03:33.225 --> 00:03:36.764
Tom and Joe were planning their new lives when they met Huck.

50
00:03:36.765 --> 00:03:39.797
Huck was also dissatisfied with his life.

51
00:03:39.798 --> 00:03:43.108
People didn't like him because his father was a drunk.

52
00:03:43.109 --> 00:03:45.959
Huck thought running away sounded fun.

53
00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:49.652
Huck helped Tom and Joe steal some food and find a log raft.

54
00:03:49.653 --> 00:03:54.765
Together they pushed the raft into the Mississippi River and headed for Jackson Island.

55
00:03:54.766 --> 00:03:58.336
Once on the island the boys became pirates.

56
00:03:58.337 --> 00:04:03.882
They took turns being their favorite pirate, and they had great battles on both land and sea.

57
00:04:03.883 --> 00:04:07.052
"Life as a pirate is great," said Huck.

58
00:04:07.053 --> 00:04:11.938
"I haven't had this much fun in ages." The other two boys agreed.

59
00:04:11.939 --> 00:04:15.303
"We should explore the island," said Joe.

60
00:04:15.304 --> 00:04:19.068
"We should look for buried treasure," shouted Tom.

61
00:04:19.069 --> 00:04:25.039
They spent the rest of the afternoon exploring the island and looking for buried treasure.

62
00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:30.232
Being a pirate was hard work, and by early evening they were tired and hungry.

63
00:04:30.233 --> 00:04:33.892
"It's time to build our camp," said Tom.

64
00:04:33.893 --> 00:04:38.644
"I think I saw some sailcloth snagged on a log," said Joe.

65
00:04:38.645 --> 00:04:41.858
"That will make an excellent tent," said Huck.

66
00:04:41.859 --> 00:04:50.250
They made a tent, cooked their food, talked around the fire, and went to sleep.

